==English==
{{wp}}

===Etymology===
{{root|en|ine-pro|*(s)kreybʰ-}}
From {{inh|en|enm|descripcioun}}, from {{der|en|fro|description}} and its etymon, {{der|en|la|dēscrīptiō}}, noun of action of {{m|la|dēscrībō||to describe}}. Equivalent to {{suf|en|describe|tion}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/dɪˈskɹɪpʃən/|/dəˈskɹɪpʃən/}}
* {{audio|en|en-us-description.ogg|a=US}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun|~}}

# A sketch or account of anything in words; a [[portraiture]] or [[representation]] in language; an enumeration of the essential qualities of a thing or species.
#: {{syn|en|portrait}}
#: {{ux|en|give a verbal '''description''' of the events}}
#: {{ux|en|a realistic '''description'''}}
# The act of [[describe|describing]]; a [[delineation]] by marks or signs.
# A set of [[characteristic]]s by which someone or something can be [[recognize]]d.
#: {{ux|en|The zoo had no lions, tigers, or cats of any '''description'''.}}
# Sort, kind.
#: {{ux|en|A dealership with cars of every '''description'''}}
# {{lb|en|taxonomy}} A scientific documentation of a [[taxon]] for the purpose of introducing it to science.
#: {{ux|en|The type '''description''' of the fungus was written by a botanist.}}
# {{lb|en|linguistics}} The act or practice of recording and describing actual language usage in a given [[speech community]], as opposed to [[prescription]], i.e. laying down norms of language usage.
# {{lb|en|linguistics}} A descriptive linguistic survey.

